==Battleground==
*1 [[Master A.]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*3 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*5 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*5 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*6 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You're going to want to bring a good counter to Master A. This may be rushers like [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]] or tankers like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera]] or [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Jamiera]]. The aku enemies are at low enough of a magnification to pose no threat, with low health and attack power. To deal with the Ottas, you can bring DPS units like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] or [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer]]. Stall and kill the Ottas, then move on to the Master A, and the stage will be over after.

